---
// CONTENT.md section 9. The work authorization line appears here and nowhere
// else on the site. No diet, calorie tracking, banking, housing, or family.
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
---
<Shell
  title="About"
  description="First-generation college student from Gujarat, now an MS Computer Science student at Northeastern. Education, earlier roles, and what I actually care about."
>
  <SectionHeading as="h1" solid="About" ghost="Me" />

  <p class="display-lede">
    I build software and I check my own work harder than anyone asks me to.
    First-generation college student from Gujarat, now doing a master's in
    computer science in Boston.
  </p>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="record-heading">
    <SectionHeading id="record-heading" solid="The" ghost="Record" />
  </section>

  <div class="card-grid card-grid-2 section-body">
    <Card>
      <h3 class="card-heading">Education</h3>
      <p class="card-body">
        B.Tech in Information Technology and Engineering at P P Savani
        University in Surat, October 2021 to May 2025, finishing at 8.32 out of
        10 with First Class with Distinction, and highest grades in Design and
        Analysis of Algorithms, Data Structures, Discrete Mathematics,
        Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, and Natural Language
        Processing.
      </p>
      <p class="card-body">
        MS in Computer Science at Northeastern's Khoury College, started January
        2026, currently at 3.7 out of 4.0, expecting to finish in May 2028.
        Coursework so far: CS 5010 Programming Design Paradigm, CS 6120 Natural
        Language Processing, and CS 5800 Algorithms.
      </p>
    </Card>

    <Card>
      <h3 class="card-heading">Work history</h3>
      <p class="card-body">
        Research assistant at P P Savani under Dr. Jayashri Patil, November 2023
        to March 2025. MERN stack developer intern at Technonite in Surat,
        December 2024 to March 2025.
      </p>
      <p class="card-body">
        At Technonite: full-stack work in MongoDB, Express, React and Node
        across e-commerce, logistics and healthcare clients. A reusable React
        component library adopted across three projects, cutting duplication and
        speeding delivery by roughly 25 percent. A real-time logistics dashboard
        on Socket.io and the Google Maps API that improved dispatch tracking by
        roughly 30 percent.
      </p>
      <p class="t-small estimates">
        Both percentages are self-reported estimates from that internship, not
        measured figures.
      </p>
    </Card>

    <Card>
      <h3 class="card-heading">Certifications</h3>
      <p class="card-body">
        AWS Fundamentals Specialization, Amazon Web Services, April 2024.
        Building Web Applications in PHP, University of Michigan, April 2024.
        Three GST courses from PwC India via Coursera, 2023.
      </p>
      <p class="card-body">
        Over 400 LeetCode problems solved, working NeetCode 150 as the spine.
      </p>
    </Card>

    <Card>
      <h3 class="card-heading">Work authorization</h3>
      <p class="card-body">
        F-1 student, CPT eligible. Earliest internship or co-op start is January
        2027. Primary target is Summer 2027.
      </p>
    </Card>
  </div>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="care-heading">
    <SectionHeading id="care-heading" solid="What I" ghost="Care About" />
    <p class="section-lede section-body">
      Whether a number can be trusted. Most of my worst bugs were not crashes.
      They were measurements that returned a plausible value under conditions
      where returning a wrong value was the only thing they could have done.
      That is why my benchmark harness refuses to answer rather than guess, and
      why the <a href="/notes">notes page</a> exists.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="interests-heading">
    <SectionHeading id="interests-heading" solid="Outside" ghost="Coursework" />
    <p class="section-lede section-body">
      Photography and cinematic colour grading, mechanical keyboard building,
      and a long-running interest in the philosophy of machine consciousness and
      technological singularity, mostly through books rather than code.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="reach-heading">
    <SectionHeading id="reach-heading" solid="Reaching" ghost="Me" />
    <ul class="links section-body">
      <li><a href="mailto:prajapati.kish@northeastern.edu">prajapati.kish@northeastern.edu</a></li>
      <li><a href="/kishan-prajapati-resume.pdf">Resume (PDF)</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/Kishan-prajapati-242">GitHub</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kishan-prajapati-617a00202">LinkedIn</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=AqL9YRcAAAAJ">Google Scholar</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://leetcode.com/u/KishanSP242">LeetCode</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Shell>

<style>
  .section-body {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .opening {
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .card-heading {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
  }

  .card-body {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
  }

  .card-body:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .estimates {
    color: var(--color-annot);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .section-lede {
    max-width: 60ch;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
  }

  .links {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
